From 5ff8db9e4ccd273d2338447ecb5c5b4611ab7eb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:39:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] aeraui: a held Back always leaves a pixel plugin

A pixel plugin takes every Back, as an Android app does, so it can run
its own navigation. Unlike Browser (Back only while it has history) or a
Host API 2 page (SET_BACK_ACTION), nothing hands Back to AERA again. With
gesture navigation off there is no bottom swipe to Home or Recents, so a
plugin that ignores BACK, or has stopped answering, traps the user.

Hold Back to leave: the Back key held down for half a second, or the edge
swipe held past the depth that accepts it for half a second before
letting go, skips the plugin and navigates back as AERA does elsewhere.
The scene is left as for Home, so the plugin is paused and stays in
Recents. A short Back still goes to the plugin. Every other scene treats
a held Back as a Back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J6XhHxrkhAcXmkzHMeCnVz
